{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class DivisibleByTwentyFive {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String s = br.readLine();\n        int n = s.length();\n        int limit = (int)Math.pow(10, n);\n        int result = 0;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < limit; i += 25) {\n            if (check(s, i)) {\n                result++;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(result);\n    }\n    \n    private static boolean check(String pattern, int value) {\n        String valStr = Integer.toString(value);\n        if (valStr.length() < pattern.length()) {\n            valStr = \"0\".repeat(pattern.length() - valStr.length()) + valStr;\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i < pattern.length(); i++) {\n            char pc = pattern.charAt(i);\n            char vc = valStr.charAt(i);\n            if (pc == 'X') continue;\n            if (pc == '_') continue;\n            if (pc != vc) return false;\n        }\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <iomanip>\n\nbool check(const std::string& pattern, int value) {\n    std::string valStr = std::to_string(value);\n    if (valStr.length() < pattern.length()) {\n        valStr = std::string(pattern.length() - valStr.length(), '0') + valStr;\n    }\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < pattern.length(); i++) {\n        char pc = pattern[i];\n        char vc = valStr[i];\n        if (pc == 'X') continue;\n        if (pc == '_') continue;\n        if (pc != vc) return false;\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::string s;\n    std::getline(std::cin, s);\n    int n = s.length();\n    int limit = static_cast<int>(std::pow(10, n));\n    int result = 0;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < limit; i += 25) {\n        if (check(s, i)) {\n            result++;\n        }\n    }\n    std::cout << result << std::endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00030214988510124385, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.8132995794294402e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.125986263010418e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.483612312673358e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -8.844937838148326e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.0014498446835204959, -0.012510042637586594, -0.01104962918907404, -5.364403477869928e-06, -1.1408897638320923, -0.4740853011608124, -0.019755156710743904, -7.390948667307384e-06, -0.00016008525562938303, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -5.1377883210079744e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -7.271740287251305e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.168244216387393e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.2159273865108844e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.766942609217949e-05, -5.960462772236